  "summary_en": "Mauritius' 2018 national AI strategy from a government working group. It reviews AI opportunities across manufacturing, healthcare, fintech, agriculture, ocean economy, transport and government, and recommends an AI Council, incentives, skills programmes, and a regulatory, ethics and data protection framework. Robotics, drones and autonomous vehicles appear only as sectoral examples.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Establish a Mauritius Artificial Intelligence Council to coordinate, monitor and fund AI projects",
   "Offer matching grants, tax credits and training grants, prioritising AI adoption over development",
   "Build AI skills via an AI campus, scholarships, reskilling and a 'talent watch'",
   "Set up a permanent ethics committee and amend data protection law",
   "Ensure humans can override AI decisions; let market players define their own liability parameters"
